### corpus/documents/emails/mite_qa_w40.md
Re: H2 mite spotting on graded eggs — need this closed out

Flagging the House 2 (24-08) mite situation from the QA side because it's now showing up in the product, not just in the barn. The graders have been pulling a steady run of eggs off H2 with mite spotting — the little dark specks and smears around the blunt end and in the pack — and the reject rate on that house has climbed enough that it's showing in the daily grade-out. Some are getting through to the case before anyone catches them.

That last part is the problem. One of Brett's accounts came back to us this week about specked eggs traced to our lot, and that's the kind of thing that puts a hold on a program or a customer visit. Even where it's cosmetic and the egg is safe, a buyer seeing bug spotting on cage-free eggs reads it as a housekeeping failure, and it's hard to un-ring that.

I've also got the UEP audit prep in front of me, and an active ectoparasite infestation with visible product contamination is exactly the kind of open item I don't want a Validus auditor finding in House 2. Karen's had the trap counts and the bird-side signs documented for months, so the paper trail already shows this was known and running.

I'm not trying to steer the treatment call — that's between you and Karen. But from where I sit this needs to actually get resolved and closed out, and soon, because it's costing us on grade-out, it's touched a customer, and it's sitting there as an audit exposure. Let me know the plan so I can note it in the file and give Brett something to take back to the account.

Anita Cho
QA / Food Safety Lead

