### corpus/documents/emails/pecking_better_w32.md
Hi,

Quick update on H4 (25-04) — they're around 52 wk now, and the pecking situation has eased off. On the last few walk-throughs I'm seeing fewer new birds getting hit; the fresh feather damage has slowed right down and it's not spreading through the house the way it looked like it might a few weeks back.

The worst individuals I'd been watching are coming along — the raw spots are scabbed over and drying, backs starting to feather back in on a few of them. Daily dead has settled back down too; we came in at 33 today and it's been sitting in that range, close to where it was before this started rather than the high 40s.

I won't say we're fully out of it, and I'll keep a close eye on it on the walk-throughs, but the house looks a lot better than it did. Wanted to close the loop and say thanks for getting on it when I flagged it.

Priya Anand
Flock Supervisor, H4–H6

